  "strategy": "We introduce a fundamentally new approach combining **gradient projection**, **dense optimization**, and **smart projection-polish cycles** to minimize the objective function \\(2n\\frac{\\|f*f\\|_\\infty}{(\\sum a)^2}\\) (lower is better). Our algorithm consists of:\n\n1. **Initialization**:\n   - Start with parent sequence if available (clamped to [0,1000])\n   - Generate diverse structures (semicircle, flattop, two bumps, exponential)\n   - Apply short clipped GD refinement with high learning rate (8000)\n   - Take only candidates with sum \u2265 0.01 and objective below 1.6\n\n2. **Structure Optimization Loop**:\n   - Maintain population of up to 10 best candidates\n   - For each initial candidate structure:\n     - Use clipped GD (2-step) with adaptive tau (minimal tau=3, adaptive min_delta=0.01)\n     - After 2 GD steps, measure improvement (delta.obj) compared to initial\n     - Set retention probability based on history of improvements\n\n3. **Aggressive Phase**:\n   - Use high-fidelity, non-smooth LP optimization with barrier methods\n   - Compute objective directly via full self-convolution (no smoothing)\n   - Incorporate careful resampling rules with maximum length 1600\n\n4. **Knowledge Distillation**:\n   - Periodically merge top performing initial structures\n   - Normalize directional improvements based on actual evaluated objectives\n   - Warm restart points at 150 and 800 steps to maintain diversity\n\nThe implementation ensures all candidates remain properly normalized, with explicit comparison of un-smoothed objectives. It incorporates these key principles:\n- Structured search space reduction\n- Real-valued gradients computed directly\n- Progressive length enforcement (clamped at [0,1600])\n- Multiple polishing strategies adapted from previous state-of-art",
